     * validation of the header, signature, and claims.
     *
     * @param encodedJWT the compact JWT representation
     * @param header     the decoded JWT header
     * @param parts      the three parts of the JWT (header, payload, signature)
     * @param verifier   the verifier used to validate the signature
     * @return the decoded {@link JWT}
     * @throws MissingVerifierException          if a signature is present but no verifier is supplied
     * @throws InvalidJWTSignatureException      if the signature is missing, invalid, or the algorithm is disallowed
     * @throws JWTExpiredException               if the token has expired
     * @throws JWTUnavailableForProcessingException if the token is not yet valid
